; physical properties: a bone is also a physical link with mass and inertia
; this bridges domain-3d and domain-physics / domain-robotics
; the bone's kona IS the joint angle — same quantity, two perspectives:
; 3D view:    quaternion rotation in scene-graph transform chain
; physics view: kona state with angular-velocity kramanusara
; in the robotics context the bone's world pose is composed from the
; scene-graph transform chain (bone.parent × bone.local = bone.world)
; the FK (forward kinematics) result IS this transform composition

(kosha bone
  (sthita domain-3d armature)
  (swarupa transform sambandha)
  (yukta quaternion parent child mass moment-of-inertia kona angular-velocity scene-graph)
  (ahara weight-paint)
  (phala vertex)
  (abheda rekha)
  (siddha fk))
